{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MRZm8gLs6R9VoUB76NXogv","type":"tool_result","content":"150\t\n151\t## AI use in issues, and the triage bot\n152\t\n153\t*Added for the triage-agent sandbox; applies to everyone who opens an issue.*\n154\t\n155\tRich receives a growing number of AI-written issues and pull requests, and new\n156\tissues are now first triaged by an automated agent. These rules apply to all\n157\tcontributors, whether or not you use AI yourself.\n158\t\n159\t### If you use AI to write an issue\n160\t\n161\t1. **Say so.** Add a line such as `AI-assisted: drafted with <tool>` at the end.\n162\t2. **Include a minimal reproducible example you ran yourself**, with its actual\n163\t   output, your Rich version and platform (`python -m rich.diagnose`). A bug report\n164\t   without a runnable example is labelled `more information needed`, however long\n165\t   its analysis.\n166\t3. **Feature requests still go to [Discussions](https://github.com/textualize/rich/discussions) first**,\n167\t   as the feature template says. An AI-written proposal does not change that.\n168\t4. Pull requests follow [AI_POLICY.md](AI_POLICY.md): fill in the template,\n169\t   name the agent you used, and link an issue or discussion where a maintainer\n170\t   approved the approach.\n171\t\n172\t### What the triage bot does and does not do\n173\t\n174\t- It runs once when an issue is opened. It may add up to three labels from"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ad031a62-8a02-42d0-9cbd-0c508971215e","uuid":"6cc70cb5-59c5-496f-800e-6c0222e5d215","timestamp":"2026-10-26T04:06:54.765Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/runner/work/OSS_A3/OSS_A3/CONTRIBUTING.md","content":"\n## AI use in issues, and the triage bot\n\n*Added for the triage-agent sandbox; applies to everyone who opens an issue.*\n\nRich receives a growing number of AI-written issues and pull requests, and new\nissues are now first triaged by an automated agent. These rules apply to all\ncontributors, whether or not you use AI yourself.\n\n### If you use AI to write an issue\n\n1. **Say so.** Add a line such as `AI-assisted: drafted with <tool>` at the end.\n2. **Include a minimal reproducible example you ran yourself**, with its actual\n   output, your Rich version and platform (`python -m rich.diagnose`). A bug report\n   without a runnable example is labelled `more information needed`, however long\n   its analysis.\n3. **Feature requests still go to [Discussions](https://github.com/textualize/rich/discussions) first**,\n   as the feature template says. An AI-written proposal does not change that.\n4. Pull requests follow [AI_POLICY.md](AI_POLICY.md): fill in the template,\n   name the agent you used, and link an issue or discussion where a maintainer\n   approved the approach.\n\n### What the triage bot does and does not do\n\n- It runs once when an issue is opened. It may add up to three labels from","numLines":25,"startLine":150,"totalLines":190}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01MRZm8gLs6R9VoUB76NXogv","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
